			"Message": "refactor(Common): Complete transport layer refactoring to PascalCase naming\n\nMajor refactoring of the transport layer in the Common crate to align with PascalCase naming conventions per CLAUDE.md. All method names and struct fields renamed from snake_case to PascalCase (e.g., `send_request` -> `SendRequest`, `correlation_id` -> `CorrelationIdentifier`).\n\nKey changes:\n- TransportStrategy trait methods renamed to PascalCase\n- UnifiedRequest/UnifiedResponse fields and methods updated\n- TransportError restructured with renamed fields\n- TransportConfig builder methods converted to PascalCase\n- Added new transport components: CircuitBreaker, Retry, Metrics\n- TransportTypeDetector now requires Send + Sync with instance methods\n- Registry simplified to remove RwLock overhead\n\nAdded new dependencies: uuid (v4), log, tokio (full), rand to support circuit breaker and retry logic. This refactoring establishes the foundation for improved transport resilience and consistency with Land's naming standards.",
			"SHA": "5264df7de05fd155d516441d3f7bad9e2a825836"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-04T07:19:06Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				276,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Common): Condense README to benefit-focused overview\n\nSimplify the Common crate README from verbose technical documentation to a concise, benefit-oriented overview. Replace 150+ lines of detailed architecture explanations, code examples, and getting started guides with bullet points emphasizing key value propositions: pure abstract traits, compile-time enforcement, and millisecond tests.\n\nKey changes:\n- Add VS Code comparison blockquote: \"VS Code's codebase imports concrete implementations directly...\"\n- Switch Rust icon from cdn.simpleicons.org to editor.land/Image/Rust.svg (branded asset)\n- Remove detailed \"ActionEffect System Explained\" with code samples\n- Remove \"Core Architecture Principles\" table\n- Remove \"Getting Started\" section with installation/usage examples\n- Condense mermaid diagram to simpler \"In the Ecosystem\" section\n- Update \"See Also\" links to point to editor.land documentation\n\nThe README now serves as a quick onboarding anchor point with links to detailed docs rather than a self-contained tutorial.",
			"SHA": "fd11100c9c2f24e69f40954798105dfc6244408a"
		},
